WEBVTT

00:00:01.022 --> 00:00:07.066
Twenty thousand leagues under the sea, by Jules Verne, retold by Fiona Bedell.

00:00:07.126 --> 00:00:08.708
Penguin readers.

00:00:08.768 --> 00:00:23.818
Level 1 Chapter 1 The Giant Whale In the year 1866, a new boat came back from sea every week with the same story.

00:00:23.878 --> 00:00:30.101
A giant whale, a hundred meters long, came near our boat, the man said.

00:00:30.162 --> 00:00:35.344
The story was in the newspapers, and a lot of people talked about it.

00:00:35.404 --> 00:00:38.785
It wasn't a whale, scientists said.

00:00:38.845 --> 00:00:43.138
A big blue whale is only 27 metres long.

00:00:43.198 --> 00:00:46.069
Perhaps it was a coral reef.

00:00:46.129 --> 00:00:53.032
But a coral reef can't send water 50 metres into the air, the seaman answered.

00:00:53.092 --> 00:00:55.634
This animal can?

00:00:55.694 --> 00:00:59.986
It went near one boat in Australian waters.

00:01:00.046 --> 00:01:05.760
Three days later, it was 700 leagues away in the Pacific.

00:01:05.819 --> 00:01:12.273
Wales can't swim 700 leagues in three days, the scientists said.

00:01:12.333 --> 00:01:15.015
Perhaps it's a submarine.

00:01:15.074 --> 00:01:19.498
But only a country with a lot of money can build a submarine.

00:01:19.557 --> 00:01:23.070
And the same answer came back from every country.

00:01:23.130 --> 00:01:26.982
We haven't got a submarine.

00:01:27.042 --> 00:01:33.293
One day, A British boat, the Scotia, was in the Atlantic.

00:01:33.353 --> 00:01:37.104
Suddenly, waters started to come into the boat.

00:01:37.164 --> 00:01:39.776
The captain looked for the problem.

00:01:39.836 --> 00:01:42.367
There was a big hole in the boat.

00:01:42.427 --> 00:01:46.169
The Scotia is very strong, he said.

00:01:46.229 --> 00:01:48.730
I don't understand this hole.

00:01:48.790 --> 00:01:51.892
Is it the work of the giant whale?

00:01:51.952 --> 00:01:59.541
To me, a French scientist, the stories of the whale were, of course, very interesting.

00:01:59.600 --> 00:02:07.158
In 1867, I visited New York, and newspapermen there asked me questions.

00:02:07.218 --> 00:02:13.250
Your famous for your book about sea animals, Mr. Aaronax, they said.

00:02:13.310 --> 00:02:16.822
What do you think about this giant whale?

00:02:16.882 --> 00:02:23.464
The sea's very big, I answered, and it's the home of many thousands of animals.

00:02:23.524 --> 00:02:27.138
Scientists don't know about all of them.

00:02:27.198 --> 00:02:31.622
But one small whale has a long spear on its head.

00:02:31.682 --> 00:02:35.342
Perhaps there's a giant whale with a spear too.

00:02:35.402 --> 00:02:40.874
And perhaps this animal's spear can make a hole in a boat.

00:02:40.934 --> 00:02:45.125
A week later, a letter arrived at my hotel.

00:02:45.185 --> 00:02:50.176
It said, you know, of course, about the giant whale.

00:02:50.236 --> 00:02:56.494
One day this whale is going to kill people, but we are going to kill it first.

00:02:56.554 --> 00:02:59.102
Please calm and look for it with us.

00:02:59.162 --> 00:03:03.872
Our boat, the Abraham Lincoln, is waiting for you.

00:03:03.932 --> 00:03:07.374
I wanted to see this interesting animal.

00:03:07.434 --> 00:03:12.965
I went quickly to the Abraham Lincoln with my Belgian servant, Consé.

00:03:13.025 --> 00:03:20.176
From New York, we went down the Atlantic coast of North and South America and into the Pacific.

00:03:20.236 --> 00:03:27.139
Week after week, all day and all night, the seamen watched the water.

00:03:27.199 --> 00:03:33.191
Conse and I watched with them, but we didn't see the giant whale.

00:03:33.251 --> 00:03:37.002
Only one man on the boat didn't watch the water.

00:03:37.062 --> 00:03:39.932
His name was Ned Land.

00:03:39.992 --> 00:03:47.934
Ned was a big, strong Canadian, about 40 years old, and he was a very good whaler.

00:03:47.994 --> 00:03:52.125
You're never going to find this whale, he said.

00:03:52.185 --> 00:03:56.707
It was near Japan in May, but it's now July.

00:03:56.767 --> 00:03:58.599
Where is it today?

00:03:58.659 --> 00:04:00.420
The Mediterranean?

00:04:00.480 --> 00:04:01.841
The Arctic?

00:04:01.901 --> 00:04:03.692
Who knows?

00:04:03.752 --> 00:04:08.115
For five long months, we looked for the whale.

00:04:08.175 --> 00:04:13.138
Then the men started to say, perhaps Ned is right.

00:04:13.198 --> 00:04:15.350
When can we go home?

00:04:15.410 --> 00:04:17.521
They asked their captain.

00:04:17.580 --> 00:04:23.424
But suddenly, one day, Ned said, there it is.

00:04:23.484 --> 00:04:26.026
I can see the giant whale.

00:04:26.086 --> 00:04:29.837
The animal moved very quickly in the water.

00:04:29.897 --> 00:04:32.498
It came near our boat.

00:04:32.558 --> 00:04:37.518
We don't want a hole in the Abraham Lincoln, the captain said.

00:04:37.578 --> 00:04:39.449
Let's move away.

00:04:39.509 --> 00:04:42.000
But our boat was slow.

00:04:42.060 --> 00:04:43.880
We watched the whale.

00:04:43.940 --> 00:04:47.141
It's going to hit us, we said.

00:04:47.201 --> 00:04:49.071
But it didn't.

00:04:49.131 --> 00:04:53.392
It went under the boat, not into it.

00:04:53.452 --> 00:04:56.702
All day we went after the whale.

00:04:56.762 --> 00:04:59.240
But it stayed in front of us.

00:04:59.300 --> 00:05:03.731
We're never going to kill this animal, the men said.

00:05:03.791 --> 00:05:06.322
It's playing games with us.

00:05:06.382 --> 00:05:10.192
But at night, the whale didn't move.

00:05:10.252 --> 00:05:14.093
Perhaps it's sleeping, Ned Lann said.

00:05:14.153 --> 00:05:15.853
Let's get near.

00:05:15.913 --> 00:05:18.084
Be very quiet.

00:05:18.144 --> 00:05:25.297
Suddenly, water from the whales back went up into the air and rained down on our boat.

00:05:25.357 --> 00:05:30.400
Then I was in the sea.

00:05:30.460 --> 00:05:40.622
Chapter 2 The Nautilus I'm not a young man, and I can't swim well.

00:05:40.682 --> 00:05:43.333
I started to go underwater.

00:05:43.393 --> 00:05:47.714
But then there was a strong hand on my back.

00:05:47.774 --> 00:05:49.754
I looked behind me.

00:05:49.814 --> 00:05:52.936
My servant was there.

00:05:52.996 --> 00:05:56.198
Why are you in the water?"

00:05:56.258 --> 00:05:57.650
I asked.

00:05:57.710 --> 00:06:02.192
You were in the sea, and I wanted to stay with you.

00:06:02.252 --> 00:06:05.304
That's my job, Mr. Aaron X.

00:06:05.364 --> 00:06:07.156
Conse said.

00:06:07.216 --> 00:06:10.549
There's a problem with the Abraham Lincoln.

00:06:10.608 --> 00:06:12.900
It can't come back for us.

00:06:12.960 --> 00:06:16.322
Let's swim and wait for morning.

00:06:16.382 --> 00:06:20.698
Before morning, my legs stopped working.

00:06:20.758 --> 00:06:24.433
Go, Conse, I said.

00:06:24.493 --> 00:06:28.684
I'm a dead man, but you're young and strong.

00:06:28.744 --> 00:06:31.064
You can find a boat."

00:06:31.124 --> 00:06:37.446
Then water came into my mouth, and my eyes closed.

00:06:37.506 --> 00:06:41.307
They opened a short time later.

00:06:41.367 --> 00:06:46.288
I was with Conse, a Ned land, too.

00:06:46.348 --> 00:06:49.448
I don't understand.

00:06:49.508 --> 00:06:51.613
We're not swimming.

00:06:51.673 --> 00:06:53.368
Where are we?"

00:06:53.428 --> 00:06:54.968
I asked.

00:06:55.028 --> 00:06:59.650
On the back of the giant whale, Ned said.

00:06:59.710 --> 00:07:01.602
Then he smiled.

00:07:01.662 --> 00:07:04.133
But it's not a whale.

00:07:04.192 --> 00:07:06.014
I looked.

00:07:06.074 --> 00:07:08.175
And he was right.

00:07:08.235 --> 00:07:11.836
We were on a submarine.

00:07:11.896 --> 00:07:18.020
You and I went into the sea at the same time, Mr. Aronax, Ned said.

00:07:18.080 --> 00:07:21.000
After that, I waited here.

00:07:21.060 --> 00:07:25.349
We're okay now, but this boat can go underwater.

00:07:25.409 --> 00:07:27.700
What are we going to do then?

00:07:27.760 --> 00:07:31.580
Suddenly, the submarine started to move.

00:07:31.640 --> 00:07:34.611
Quickly, I said, make some noise.

00:07:34.671 --> 00:07:37.532
Hit the boat with your hands.

00:07:37.592 --> 00:07:42.213
A door opened and eight men came out.

00:07:42.273 --> 00:07:45.264
We went with them into the submarine.

00:07:45.324 --> 00:07:47.384
Where are you taking us?

00:07:47.444 --> 00:07:51.282
We asked the men, but they didn't answer.

00:07:51.342 --> 00:07:54.040
We arrived in a dark room.

00:07:54.100 --> 00:07:58.432
The men went away and closed the door behind them.

00:07:58.492 --> 00:08:02.154
Ned tried the door, but it didn't open.

00:08:02.174 --> 00:08:06.146
We were never going to escape, he said.

00:08:06.206 --> 00:08:09.418
Those men are going to kill us.

00:08:09.478 --> 00:08:13.830
We waited for a long time in the dark room.

00:08:13.890 --> 00:08:18.823
Then the lights came on and a man walked into the room.

00:08:18.883 --> 00:08:23.485
Perhaps he was 35, or perhaps 50.

00:08:23.545 --> 00:08:29.858
He was tall with black eyes and an interesting open face.

00:08:29.918 --> 00:08:36.222
In French, I said our names and asked for food and drink.

00:08:36.282 --> 00:08:38.363
He listened quietly.

00:08:38.423 --> 00:08:40.864
But he didn't answer.

00:08:40.924 --> 00:08:44.496
He doesn't understand French, I said.

00:08:44.556 --> 00:08:46.107
You try, Ned.

00:08:46.167 --> 00:08:48.582
Perhaps he understands English.

00:08:48.642 --> 00:08:53.400
Ned talked in English, then Conse tried in German.

00:08:53.460 --> 00:08:56.401
But they had the same problem.

00:08:56.461 --> 00:08:58.802
What can we do now?

00:08:58.862 --> 00:09:00.574
I asked my friends.

00:09:00.634 --> 00:09:04.516
But the man walked away and closed the door.

00:09:04.576 --> 00:09:06.997
Again we waited.

00:09:07.057 --> 00:09:09.548
Ned was very angry.

00:09:09.608 --> 00:09:12.360
He didn't like the men on the submarine.

00:09:12.420 --> 00:09:14.471
He didn't like our room.

00:09:14.531 --> 00:09:17.338
And he didn't like waiting.

00:09:17.397 --> 00:09:22.586
I'm going to escape from this submarine," he said.

00:09:22.646 --> 00:09:28.620
A man came into the room, and Ned started to hit him in the face.

00:09:28.680 --> 00:09:33.942
Can't say and I wanted to stop Ned, but he was very strong.

00:09:34.002 --> 00:09:37.814
Suddenly, our first visitor was with us again.

00:09:37.874 --> 00:09:39.186
Stop!

00:09:39.246 --> 00:09:40.796
Mr. Land?

00:09:40.856 --> 00:09:43.858
He said, in very good French.

00:09:43.918 --> 00:09:47.499
And please, listen to me, all of you.

00:09:47.559 --> 00:09:54.183
My name is Captain Nemo, and this is my boat, the Nautilus.

00:09:54.243 --> 00:09:57.516
I didn't talk to you on my first visit.

00:09:57.576 --> 00:10:02.100
I'm sorry about that, but you're a problem for me.

00:10:02.160 --> 00:10:04.982
What can I do with you?

00:10:05.042 --> 00:10:09.146
My men and I are never going back to our countries.

00:10:09.206 --> 00:10:12.538
We're always going to live on the Nautilus.

00:10:12.598 --> 00:10:15.098
You can live with us too.

00:10:15.158 --> 00:10:18.858
But you can't go back to your countries after that.

00:10:18.918 --> 00:10:22.800
We don't want stories in the newspapers about us.

00:10:22.860 --> 00:10:24.772
What are you saying?"

00:10:24.832 --> 00:10:26.062
I asked.

00:10:26.123 --> 00:10:28.354
We want to go home.

00:10:28.414 --> 00:10:31.696
You can go now, he answered.

00:10:31.756 --> 00:10:36.230
But it's going to be difficult for you, because you haven't got a boat.

00:10:36.290 --> 00:10:40.363
You're underwater, and you aren't near the coast.

00:10:40.422 --> 00:10:45.437
Stay with us now, and you can see a lot of interesting things.

00:10:45.497 --> 00:10:50.131
but you can never go home.

00:10:50.191 --> 00:10:59.569
Chapter 3 Our first weeks underwater We stayed, of course.

00:10:59.629 --> 00:11:03.382
We walked with Nemo's men to our new bedrooms.

00:11:03.442 --> 00:11:06.484
Then I had some food with the captain.

00:11:06.544 --> 00:11:12.810
Our food comes from the sea, he said, and we eat very well.

00:11:12.870 --> 00:11:22.408
Our shirts, our shoes, Our beds, our pens, we make all of them from sea animals too.

00:11:22.468 --> 00:11:24.630
I love the sea.

00:11:24.690 --> 00:11:26.890
It's our only friend.

00:11:26.950 --> 00:11:31.022
People can't make problems for us here.

00:11:31.082 --> 00:11:34.844
But you don't want to listen to me all day.

00:11:34.904 --> 00:11:38.156
Come and see my submarine.

00:11:38.216 --> 00:11:42.454
We went into a room with thousands of books.

00:11:42.514 --> 00:11:48.411
I often read your book about sea animals, Mr. Aaronax, the captain said.

00:11:48.471 --> 00:11:55.703
You write very well, but your time on the Nautilus is going to teach you a lot of new things.

00:11:55.763 --> 00:12:00.745
A submarine is a good home for a scientist.

00:12:00.805 --> 00:12:07.887
I visited every room on the Nautilus, the first and only submarine in the seas.

00:12:07.947 --> 00:12:10.383
Captain Nemo was its builder.

00:12:10.443 --> 00:12:15.039
and he talked about his answers to the problems of an underwater boat.

00:12:15.099 --> 00:12:20.540
He was a clever scientist, and a very interesting man.

00:12:20.600 --> 00:12:26.102
Later, Ned and Conse asked me about Captain Nemo.

00:12:26.162 --> 00:12:27.743
Who was he?

00:12:27.802 --> 00:12:29.393
Where did he come from?

00:12:29.453 --> 00:12:33.564
Why did he stay away from people and live underwater?

00:12:33.624 --> 00:12:37.918
But I didn't know the answers to their questions.

00:12:37.978 --> 00:12:46.238
Then, suddenly, the nautilus's sea lights came on, and we stopped thinking about the captain.

00:12:46.298 --> 00:12:54.514
The sea looked very beautiful, with fish of every colour, big and small.

00:12:54.574 --> 00:12:58.836
We didn't take our eyes from the sea all night.

00:12:58.896 --> 00:13:01.528
Captain Nemo was right.

00:13:01.589 --> 00:13:07.136
A submarine was a good home for a scientist.

00:13:07.196 --> 00:13:12.061
The weeks after that were quiet, but interesting.

00:13:12.121 --> 00:13:16.772
The submarine usually stayed about 100 metres underwater.

00:13:16.832 --> 00:13:24.594
But every morning we went up for air, and my friends and I looked across the blue waters of the Pacific.

00:13:24.654 --> 00:13:33.097
We didn't often see Captain Nemo, but Conse and I looked at his books and at the fish in the sea.

00:13:33.157 --> 00:13:35.846
Only Ned was unhappy.

00:13:35.906 --> 00:13:43.556
He wasn't a scientist, and he didn't like reading, and he didn't like eating fish every day.

00:13:43.616 --> 00:13:50.268
One day, Captain Nemo said, there are a lot of animals in the trees of Crespo.

00:13:50.328 --> 00:13:52.419
They make good food.

00:13:52.479 --> 00:13:55.200
Do you want to look for some with me?

00:13:55.260 --> 00:13:58.221
Trees, I asked.

00:13:58.281 --> 00:14:00.382
Are we near the coast?

00:14:00.442 --> 00:14:05.309
There are underwater trees, he answered.

00:14:05.369 --> 00:14:15.438
Ned didn't want to come, but Konsai and I dressed in diving suits and walked on the sea floor with the captain and his men.

00:14:15.498 --> 00:14:17.630
It wasn't difficult.

00:14:17.690 --> 00:14:23.532
On a boat, diving suits are heavy, but they are light in the water.

00:14:23.592 --> 00:14:25.933
There was only one problem.

00:14:25.993 --> 00:14:34.740
I wanted to talk about the tall trees and beautiful fish with Konsai, but you can't hear people in a diving suit.

00:14:34.800 --> 00:14:45.243
Captain Nemo and his men killed some big animals, and we went back to the Nautilus, with a lot of good food.

00:14:45.303 --> 00:14:48.846
Chapter 4.

00:14:48.906 --> 00:14:56.984
Papua Spears After two months on the Nautilus, we were near the coast of Australia.

00:14:57.044 --> 00:15:03.250
Captain Nemo wanted to take us to Asia, but the seas in front of us were very difficult.

00:15:03.310 --> 00:15:11.658
The coral reefs are famous because they are beautiful, but they are famous too because boats often hit them.

00:15:11.718 --> 00:15:16.510
There are a lot of dead seamen in those waters.

00:15:16.570 --> 00:15:22.474
We went slowly and looked for coral reefs under the water in front of us.

00:15:22.534 --> 00:15:26.276
For a long time we didn't have any problems.

00:15:26.336 --> 00:15:30.498
Then, suddenly, there was a big noise.

00:15:30.558 --> 00:15:32.916
The nautilus stopped.

00:15:32.976 --> 00:15:34.662
What's wrong?"

00:15:34.722 --> 00:15:36.444
I asked the captain.

00:15:36.504 --> 00:15:40.286
The nautilus is sitting on a coral reef.

00:15:40.346 --> 00:15:42.308
It can't move.

00:15:42.368 --> 00:15:44.558
He answered quietly.

00:15:44.618 --> 00:15:46.890
But it's not a problem.

00:15:46.950 --> 00:15:51.684
After five days, the sea's going to take us away from here.

00:15:51.744 --> 00:15:58.928
The sea goes up and down every day, of course, and it goes up and down every month, too.

00:15:58.988 --> 00:16:01.861
Was Captain Nemo right?

00:16:01.921 --> 00:16:05.676
Ned didn't want to wait and see.

00:16:05.736 --> 00:16:09.699
We can escape from the Nautilus today, he said.

00:16:09.758 --> 00:16:11.310
The coast is near.

00:16:11.370 --> 00:16:12.541
Let's go!

00:16:12.601 --> 00:16:15.464
No, Ned, I answered.

00:16:15.524 --> 00:16:17.786
The papuans live on that coast.

00:16:17.846 --> 00:16:21.798
Papuans often kill and eat their visitors.

00:16:21.858 --> 00:16:27.134
Every day, Ned looked across the water at the beautiful coast.

00:16:27.194 --> 00:16:32.370
Perhaps we can go there and look for food, he said.

00:16:32.430 --> 00:16:39.448
We asked the captain, though of course you can go, he said, with a smile.

00:16:39.508 --> 00:16:44.522
Take the little boat, but be back here before night time.

00:16:44.582 --> 00:16:52.148
Ned, Conse and I arrived on the coast, and for a long time we didn't stop eating.

00:16:52.208 --> 00:16:57.842
There was a lot of fruit on the trees, and it was very good.

00:16:57.902 --> 00:17:01.306
Conse and I looked at the beautiful animals.

00:17:01.366 --> 00:17:06.718
Ned looked at the animals too, but he wanted them for food.

00:17:06.778 --> 00:17:14.480
He worked quickly, and that evening we had a lot of dead animals and fruit for the Nautilus's kitchen.

00:17:14.540 --> 00:17:23.692
We started to put things in the little boat, but suddenly Conse said, Oh, what was that on my hand?

00:17:23.752 --> 00:17:28.063
Look, Ned said, there are men in the trees.

00:17:28.123 --> 00:17:29.864
They've got spears.

00:17:29.924 --> 00:17:31.894
They're going to kill us.

00:17:31.954 --> 00:17:37.425
Conse and I were quickly in the boat, but Ned wanted to get the food first.

00:17:37.485 --> 00:17:41.266
A rain of small spears came from the trees.

00:17:41.326 --> 00:17:45.468
Then one hundred men started to run to our boat.

00:17:45.528 --> 00:17:49.368
We went quickly across the water to the Nautilus.

00:17:49.428 --> 00:17:54.320
The papuins stayed on the coast because they didn't have boats.

00:17:54.380 --> 00:18:01.673
In the morning, there were six hundred papuans on the coast, and some of them had boats.

00:18:01.734 --> 00:18:04.696
They came across the sea to the nautilus.

00:18:04.756 --> 00:18:09.158
We've got a big problem now, I said, to Captain Nemo.

00:18:09.218 --> 00:18:14.521
The papuans can't get into the nautilus today, because the doors are closed.

00:18:14.581 --> 00:18:20.254
But tomorrow there isn't going to be any air in here, because we can't open the doors.

00:18:20.314 --> 00:18:22.359
What are we going to do then?

00:18:22.419 --> 00:18:25.546
Captain Nemo didn't look unhappy.

00:18:25.606 --> 00:18:30.149
We're going to wait and see, he said.

00:18:30.209 --> 00:18:33.222
I didn't sleep well that night.

00:18:33.282 --> 00:18:37.034
In the morning there were a lot of papuins on the Nautilus.

00:18:37.095 --> 00:18:39.796
There wasn't much air for us now.

00:18:39.856 --> 00:18:43.070
But the doors stayed closed.

00:18:43.130 --> 00:18:47.714
We're going this afternoon, the captain said.

00:18:47.774 --> 00:18:55.523
That afternoon, after five days on the coral reef, The nautilus suddenly started to move.

00:18:55.583 --> 00:18:58.004
Captain Nemo was right.

00:18:58.064 --> 00:19:02.718
The sea was up, and the submarine was in water again.

00:19:02.778 --> 00:19:05.480
We moved quickly away from the coast.

00:19:05.540 --> 00:19:09.312
We looked back, and the papuins were in the sea.

00:19:09.372 --> 00:19:17.268
Then we opened the doors, and air came into the boat.

00:19:17.328 --> 00:19:29.199
Chapter 5 Nemo's Gold We went across Indian and Arabian waters and into the Red Sea.

00:19:29.259 --> 00:19:33.910
Ned didn't stop thinking about escape from the Nautilus.

00:19:33.971 --> 00:19:36.571
Where are we going after this?

00:19:36.631 --> 00:19:37.962
He asked.

00:19:38.022 --> 00:19:45.103
Back to the Arabian Sea first, I answered, then perhaps down the African coast.

00:19:45.163 --> 00:19:48.414
But we didn't go back to the Arabian Sea.

00:19:48.474 --> 00:19:55.629
One day, Captain Nemo said, Tomorrow, We're going to be in the Mediterranean.

00:19:55.689 --> 00:19:57.820
I didn't understand.

00:19:57.880 --> 00:20:03.541
We can't go from the Red Sea to the Mediterranean in a boat, I said.

00:20:03.601 --> 00:20:07.602
How are we going to take the Nautilus across Egypt?

00:20:07.662 --> 00:20:11.393
We aren't going to go across Egypt.

00:20:11.453 --> 00:20:15.764
We're going to go under it, the captain answered.

00:20:15.824 --> 00:20:19.005
I know an underwater tunnel.

00:20:19.065 --> 00:20:22.734
That evening, we went into the tunnel.

00:20:22.794 --> 00:20:26.092
It was very dark and very small.

00:20:26.152 --> 00:20:31.735
But Nemo was a good seaman, and the Nautilus didn't have any problems.

00:20:31.795 --> 00:20:36.868
In a very short time, we were in the Mediterranean.

00:20:36.928 --> 00:20:40.689
We then moved quickly away from Egypt.

00:20:40.749 --> 00:20:44.891
Near Crete, I remembered stories in the newspapers.

00:20:44.951 --> 00:20:47.392
Crete was in Turkey.

00:20:47.452 --> 00:20:50.404
But the Creteans wanted to be Greek.

00:20:50.464 --> 00:20:57.100
A lot of Cretans were now dead, because the Turkish people were very angry with them.

00:20:57.160 --> 00:20:59.451
I looked at the sea.

00:20:59.511 --> 00:21:04.624
There was a swimmer underwater, and he didn't have a diving suit.

00:21:04.684 --> 00:21:11.117
Quickly, I said to Captain Nemo, let's go to him now, or the sea's going to kill him.

00:21:11.178 --> 00:21:14.519
He's okay, the captain answered.

00:21:14.580 --> 00:21:19.540
His name's Nicholas, and he's a very good swimmer.

00:21:19.600 --> 00:21:22.860
Was this man a friend of the captain?

00:21:22.920 --> 00:21:28.186
I wanted to ask, but then I stopped thinking about the swimmer.

00:21:28.246 --> 00:21:32.712
Captain Nemo had gold in his hands.

00:21:32.772 --> 00:21:38.378
I looked behind him, and there was gold on the table too.

00:21:38.438 --> 00:21:41.444
A lot of gold.

00:21:41.504 --> 00:21:45.551
Later, I listened to the noises of the night.

00:21:45.611 --> 00:21:51.885
Men went away from the nautilus in a little boat, and came back a short time later.

00:21:51.946 --> 00:21:54.938
Did they take gold with them?

00:21:54.998 --> 00:21:57.550
Where did they take it?

00:21:57.610 --> 00:22:00.842
Was it for the Kritans?

00:22:00.902 --> 00:22:08.247
We didn't go near any coasts after this, and three days later we were in the Atlantic.

00:22:08.307 --> 00:22:09.976
Ned was angry.

00:22:10.036 --> 00:22:16.536
He wanted to escape to a European country, and Europe was behind us now.

00:22:16.596 --> 00:22:21.277
But first, we went up the coast of Portugal and Spain.

00:22:21.337 --> 00:22:25.229
We're going to escape this evening, Ned said.

00:22:25.289 --> 00:22:31.271
Meet Consé and me at the little boat at nine o'clock.

00:22:31.291 --> 00:22:36.490
I wanted to stay on the Nautilus, because it was a good home for a scientist.

00:22:36.550 --> 00:22:44.650
But I wanted to see Paris again one day, and this was perhaps the only time for an escape.

00:22:44.710 --> 00:22:48.521
Okay, I said to Ned.

00:22:48.582 --> 00:22:55.564
At nine o'clock I opened my door and started to walk to the little boat.

00:22:55.625 --> 00:23:03.128
But suddenly did Nautilus stop on the sea floor, then Captain Nemo arrived.

00:23:03.188 --> 00:23:10.236
He wanted the answer to a question I think, Mr. Aaronax, he said.

00:23:10.296 --> 00:23:11.587
Come with me!

00:23:11.607 --> 00:23:15.580
I went with him to the window.

00:23:15.640 --> 00:23:22.764
There were some old boats on the sea floor, and Nemo's men were there in their diving suits.

00:23:22.824 --> 00:23:29.119
They walked to the old boats, and came back with gold in their hands.

00:23:29.179 --> 00:23:34.058
These boats went down to the sea floor in 1702.

00:23:34.118 --> 00:23:37.644
heavy with South American gold.

00:23:37.704 --> 00:23:42.346
My men and I sometimes come here and take a little gold.

00:23:42.406 --> 00:23:44.646
But it isn't for us.

00:23:44.706 --> 00:23:49.327
There are unhappy people in many countries.

00:23:49.387 --> 00:23:52.148
The gold is for them.

00:23:52.208 --> 00:23:59.950
I remembered the problems in Crete and started to understand Captain Nemo.

00:24:00.010 --> 00:24:03.362
But Ned was not a happy man.

00:24:03.422 --> 00:24:05.176
Where were you?"

00:24:05.236 --> 00:24:06.867
he asked me later.

00:24:06.927 --> 00:24:12.350
We waited for you, but you didn't come.

00:24:12.410 --> 00:24:23.577
Chapter 6 To The South Pole A day later, we were many leagues from the coast.

00:24:23.637 --> 00:24:29.340
The roads here are very bad, Mr. Aaronax, Captain Nemo said.

00:24:29.400 --> 00:24:32.368
But do you want to walk on them with me?

00:24:32.428 --> 00:24:36.106
roads under the sea.

00:24:36.166 --> 00:24:42.497
I didn't understand, but I put on my diving suit and went with the captain.

00:24:42.557 --> 00:24:45.808
Nemo walked quickly underwater.

00:24:45.868 --> 00:24:50.549
I wanted to stay with him, but it was very difficult.

00:24:50.609 --> 00:24:56.550
My feet came down on the sea floor, but the sea floor moved with me.

00:24:56.610 --> 00:24:59.621
What was under my feet?

00:24:59.681 --> 00:25:03.650
For a long time we didn't stop walking.

00:25:03.710 --> 00:25:08.758
And then I had the answer to my question.

00:25:08.818 --> 00:25:13.510
There were old houses on the sea floor.

00:25:13.570 --> 00:25:21.164
But why were there buildings here in the Atlantic under 300 metres of water?

00:25:21.224 --> 00:25:23.824
The sea floor went up.

00:25:23.884 --> 00:25:31.980
Captain Nemo stopped walking and started to write with his hand in the water.

00:25:32.040 --> 00:25:36.382
Atlantis.

00:25:36.442 --> 00:25:44.967
There were many stories about this underwater country, but for many people they were only stories.

00:25:45.027 --> 00:25:46.948
I looked down.

00:25:47.008 --> 00:25:51.190
There was a big town on the sea floor.

00:25:51.250 --> 00:25:54.321
For a long time I didn't move.

00:25:54.381 --> 00:26:00.474
I was one of the first people in Atlantis for hundreds of years.

00:26:00.534 --> 00:26:04.583
I wanted to remember it.

00:26:04.643 --> 00:26:10.393
After our visit to Atlantis, the Nautilus didn't stop.

00:26:10.453 --> 00:26:13.674
For many weeks the sun was very strong.

00:26:13.734 --> 00:26:18.717
Then the air started to get cold, and there was ice in the sea.

00:26:18.777 --> 00:26:21.958
We were in the seas of the Antarctic.

00:26:22.018 --> 00:26:26.801
Four days after the first ice, the Nautilus stopped.

00:26:26.861 --> 00:26:32.870
There was ice in front of us, and ice behind us.

00:26:32.930 --> 00:26:37.386
We can't move, Ned said to concet in me.

00:26:37.446 --> 00:26:40.668
How are we going to escape from the ice?

00:26:40.728 --> 00:26:48.210
But Captain Nemo came to us and said, we're going to be the first people at the South Pole.

00:26:48.270 --> 00:26:53.612
We can get there in a submarine, because there's water under this ice.

00:26:53.672 --> 00:26:55.932
There's only one problem.

00:26:55.992 --> 00:26:59.025
We can't come up for air.

00:26:59.085 --> 00:27:04.630
The Nautilus went down and down.

00:27:04.690 --> 00:27:12.914
At 300 metres, we were under the ice, and there was water in front of us again.

00:27:12.974 --> 00:27:17.076
We started to move quickly to the South Pole.

00:27:17.136 --> 00:27:22.178
After a day, we were under 1,000 metres of ice.

00:27:22.239 --> 00:27:29.094
But the morning after that, there were only 50 metres of ice, then 20.

00:27:29.154 --> 00:27:31.559
Ten.

00:27:31.619 --> 00:27:34.170
Five.

00:27:34.231 --> 00:27:40.524
And then the Nautilus came up into the air and the open sea.

00:27:40.584 --> 00:27:44.396
We were at the South Pole.

00:27:44.456 --> 00:27:46.888
It wasn't very cold.

00:27:46.948 --> 00:27:50.450
Perhaps three degrees centigrade.

00:27:50.510 --> 00:27:57.284
We stayed there for three happy days and looked at a lot of interesting animals and fish.

00:27:57.345 --> 00:28:00.414
Then we went under the ice again.

00:28:00.474 --> 00:28:04.153
That night, there was a big noise.

00:28:04.213 --> 00:28:11.895
Captain Nemo said, the ice moved at the wrong time, and now we've got a problem.

00:28:11.955 --> 00:28:18.707
We're under 300 metres of ice, but there's ice under us too.

00:28:18.767 --> 00:28:22.578
And on our left, and right.

00:28:22.638 --> 00:28:30.592
We're in a tunnel, but in front of us there's water, and it's going to take us up to the air.

00:28:30.652 --> 00:28:36.248
The Nautilus moved quickly in the tunnel, but then there was a noise again.

00:28:36.308 --> 00:28:39.430
There was now ice in front of us, too.

00:28:39.490 --> 00:28:42.304
The Nautilus started to go back.

00:28:42.364 --> 00:28:44.496
The same noise.

00:28:44.556 --> 00:28:46.928
Ice behind us.

00:28:46.988 --> 00:28:51.442
We're all dead, Ned Land said.

00:28:51.502 --> 00:28:56.266
We've got air for two days, Captain Nemo answered.

00:28:56.326 --> 00:28:59.080
After that, who knows?

00:28:59.140 --> 00:29:03.015
but there are only 10 meters of ice under the nautilus.

00:29:03.075 --> 00:29:05.986
Under that, there's water again.

00:29:06.047 --> 00:29:15.682
We can make a hole in the ice with knives and spears, and the nautilus can escape from the tunnel into open water.

00:29:15.742 --> 00:29:24.166
We dressed in diving suits and started to work with the knives and spears, but it was a big job.

00:29:24.226 --> 00:29:27.014
Perhaps four or five days' work.

00:29:27.074 --> 00:29:30.423
and we didn't have five days.

00:29:30.484 --> 00:29:36.216
After three days we were all ill because there wasn't any new air.

00:29:36.276 --> 00:29:39.067
But we didn't stop working.

00:29:39.127 --> 00:29:41.398
Captain Nemo worked with us.

00:29:41.458 --> 00:29:46.110
Then he said, into the submarine, all of you.

00:29:46.171 --> 00:29:49.622
There are only two meters of ice under us now.

00:29:49.682 --> 00:29:53.943
The Nautilus is going to do our work for us.

00:29:54.004 --> 00:29:56.915
The Nautilus was strong and heavy.

00:29:56.975 --> 00:30:01.206
It went down into our hole again and again.

00:30:01.266 --> 00:30:07.900
The ice started to move, and suddenly we were in open water.

00:30:07.960 --> 00:30:15.192
But there wasn't any air on the boat, and we were all very ill.

00:30:15.252 --> 00:30:18.374
The nautilus moved under the ice.

00:30:18.434 --> 00:30:21.586
We waited and waited.

00:30:21.646 --> 00:30:26.410
I closed my eyes and started to sleep.

00:30:26.470 --> 00:30:29.536
Or was I dead?

00:30:29.596 --> 00:30:33.510
Then suddenly my eyes opened.

00:30:33.570 --> 00:30:35.421
What was that noise?

00:30:35.481 --> 00:30:42.338
The Nautilus is hitting ice again, but this ice is thin, conce said.

00:30:42.398 --> 00:30:45.612
Perhaps we're going to be okay.

00:30:45.672 --> 00:30:49.264
The Nautilus tried again and again.

00:30:49.324 --> 00:30:52.203
First there were small holes in the ice.

00:30:52.263 --> 00:30:55.294
Then suddenly there was one big hole.

00:30:55.354 --> 00:30:57.904
The Nautilus went up into it.

00:30:57.964 --> 00:31:00.305
We weren't dead.

00:31:00.365 --> 00:31:04.866
We had air.

00:31:04.926 --> 00:31:11.308
Chapter 7 Goodbye to the Nautilus.

00:31:11.368 --> 00:31:17.448
After our visit to the Antarctic, we didn't see Captain Nemo very often.

00:31:17.508 --> 00:31:21.927
The Nautilus went up the coast of South and North America.

00:31:21.987 --> 00:31:26.848
We wanted to escape, but every night there was a problem.

00:31:26.908 --> 00:31:31.338
We weren't near the coast, or the sea was difficult.

00:31:31.398 --> 00:31:37.719
Then we went across the Atlantic to Europe and arrived in British waters.

00:31:37.779 --> 00:31:41.080
Suddenly there was a big noise.

00:31:41.140 --> 00:31:42.400
Boom!

00:31:42.460 --> 00:31:44.600
We looked across the sea.

00:31:44.661 --> 00:31:47.974
There was a big boat three leagues away.

00:31:48.034 --> 00:31:50.849
"'It was that boat,' Ned said.

00:31:50.869 --> 00:31:54.632
"'It wants to hit the Nautilus and kill us all.'

00:31:54.652 --> 00:31:57.724
"'Which country is it from?'

00:31:57.784 --> 00:31:58.555
I asked.

00:31:58.575 --> 00:32:02.278
"'I can't see,' Ned answered.

00:32:02.298 --> 00:32:03.959
"'Boom!'

00:32:04.019 --> 00:32:08.672
Water went up into the air only five metres from the Nautilus.

00:32:08.732 --> 00:32:11.114
Captain Nemo arrived.

00:32:11.174 --> 00:32:14.728
He was very angry, and he didn't look at us.

00:32:14.788 --> 00:32:25.398
He looked at the boat across the water and said, First, you take my country and my family, and now you want to kill me too.

00:32:25.458 --> 00:32:28.560
But can you find me underwater?

00:32:28.620 --> 00:32:29.870
No.

00:32:29.931 --> 00:32:35.834
The Nautilus is going to hit your boat and kill you all.

00:32:35.894 --> 00:32:40.317
I wanted to stop the captain, but he didn't listen to me.

00:32:40.378 --> 00:32:45.360
The Nautilus moved away from the coast, and the boat came after us.

00:32:45.420 --> 00:32:47.928
Then we went underwater.

00:32:47.988 --> 00:32:50.896
For a short time it was quiet.

00:32:50.956 --> 00:32:54.077
Then we started to move very quickly.

00:32:54.137 --> 00:32:56.568
Suddenly the boat was in front of us.

00:32:56.628 --> 00:32:59.220
The Nautilus went into it.

00:32:59.280 --> 00:33:02.610
There was a big hole in the boat now.

00:33:02.671 --> 00:33:09.203
A lot of water went in, and the boat started to go down slowly under the sea.

00:33:09.264 --> 00:33:12.985
There were hundreds of men in the water.

00:33:13.045 --> 00:33:16.770
Captain Nemo watched them quietly.

00:33:16.830 --> 00:33:19.347
in a short time.

00:33:19.407 --> 00:33:22.510
They were all dead.

00:33:22.570 --> 00:33:26.664
Nemo went back to his bedroom.

00:33:26.724 --> 00:33:29.807
I looked at him from the door.

00:33:29.867 --> 00:33:39.076
He was on the floor, and in his hands there was a photograph of a beautiful young woman and two small children.

00:33:39.136 --> 00:33:41.900
His dead family.

00:33:41.960 --> 00:33:49.988
After that unhappy day, we went up the coasts of Britain and Norway and into the seas of the Arctic.

00:33:50.048 --> 00:33:56.312
For a week, Ned Conse and I didn't see Captain Nemo and his men.

00:33:56.372 --> 00:34:01.306
Then one day Ned said, I can see the coast.

00:34:01.366 --> 00:34:06.410
It isn't near, but I can't stay on the Nautilus.

00:34:06.470 --> 00:34:10.990
I want to be home, or dead in the sea.

00:34:11.050 --> 00:34:14.718
I wanted to be away from the submarine, too.

00:34:14.778 --> 00:34:17.708
You're right, Ned, I answered.

00:34:17.768 --> 00:34:21.219
Let's escape this evening."

00:34:21.239 --> 00:34:23.780
I'm going to put food in the little boat.

00:34:23.840 --> 00:34:26.670
Be there at ten, he said.

00:34:26.731 --> 00:34:30.491
At ten o'clock, I went to the little boat.

00:34:30.551 --> 00:34:33.572
Ned and Conse were there before me.

00:34:33.632 --> 00:34:38.510
Okay, put the boat in the water, Ned said.

00:34:38.570 --> 00:34:42.030
But suddenly there were noises from Nemo's men.

00:34:42.090 --> 00:34:44.511
Did they know about our escape?

00:34:44.572 --> 00:34:46.402
The maelstrom!

00:34:46.462 --> 00:34:48.344
The maelstrom!"

00:34:48.404 --> 00:34:50.034
The men said.

00:34:50.095 --> 00:34:53.207
This was a big problem.

00:34:53.267 --> 00:34:56.118
All seamen know about the maelstrom.

00:34:56.178 --> 00:35:02.652
Some of the seas of the arctic move very quickly, and in one place two of those seas meet.

00:35:02.712 --> 00:35:06.256
There, a giant hole opens in the water.

00:35:06.316 --> 00:35:10.739
Boats and whales, tang leagues away, can't escape it.

00:35:10.799 --> 00:35:14.871
The maelstrom takes them all down to the sea floor.

00:35:14.932 --> 00:35:18.424
The maelstrom now wanted the nautilus.

00:35:18.484 --> 00:35:21.845
We looked at the big hole in the sea in front of us.

00:35:21.905 --> 00:35:26.328
The maelstrom's going to kill us, we said.

00:35:26.388 --> 00:35:31.420
There was a noise, and our little boat went into the sea.

00:35:31.480 --> 00:35:33.456
I went in too.

00:35:33.516 --> 00:35:36.672
My head went under the water.

00:35:36.732 --> 00:35:40.125
Then my eyes closed.

00:35:40.185 --> 00:35:42.858
I opened my eyes.

00:35:42.918 --> 00:35:46.040
Ned and Conse were there.

00:35:46.100 --> 00:35:51.364
We were in the house of a Norwegian seaman.

00:35:51.424 --> 00:35:54.286
How did we get here?

00:35:54.346 --> 00:35:56.398
We don't remember.

00:35:56.458 --> 00:35:59.748
But in a short time we can go home.

00:35:59.808 --> 00:36:03.287
Every day we talk about the Nautilus.

00:36:03.347 --> 00:36:05.707
We have a lot of questions.

00:36:05.767 --> 00:36:09.388
But perhaps we are never going to know the answers.

00:36:09.448 --> 00:36:12.739
Where did Captain Nemo come from?

00:36:12.799 --> 00:36:15.349
Who killed his family?

00:36:15.409 --> 00:36:20.370
Did he and his men escape from the maelstrom?

00:36:20.430 --> 00:36:22.781
And where is he now?

